From 5afc5f2e0f0c244573500a09de0fb92edd6f1179 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Lakr233 <git@qaq.wiki>
Date: Fri, 13 Nov 2026 15:53:25 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 78/79] vgpu: keep what inplace_copy_lph writes to a heap
 texture

Component: Vulkan draw, fragment storage images and sampled heap
textures.

macOS 27 snapshots the framebuffer under a window's and a menu's
rounded corners with inplace_copy_lph, a fragment shader with no colour
output that writes a storage image. Its target is a heap texture
(opcode 0x38, 42x42 and 54x54 RGBA16F). The storage-image rail kept
texels only for a linear texture; for a heap texture the shader wrote a
scratch image that was dropped, and the corners sampled 0076's
transparent black. Windows and menus drew with black corners.

A heap texture has no guest bytes, so what the shader writes now goes
to DeviceState::heap_snapshots, keyed by task, reference and lifetime
generation, and the image is seeded from the snapshot or the pass's
resident. A sampled heap texture serves its snapshot ahead of the
resident, and a pass that draws into the texture drops the snapshot.

Measured on arm64 Linux (NVIDIA GB10), macOS 27.2 guest at protocol 237,
cold boots: before, About This Mac and both menus had black corners;
after, 163 snapshots written and 2012 sampled in one boot, and the
corners are rounded over the desktop.

Verified: the reims-vgpu test suite passes, with two new tests for the
sampled snapshot; clippy unchanged.
Not verified: the backend-metal arm (this rail is Vulkan-only).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
